        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d9b74ff9d22f429981920ffd84ccb35d",
      "statement": "A Bandai-Namco BVH's rest Hips OFFSET records capture-volume placement rather than anatomy and varies from clip to clip — three values within dataset-2 alone, up to 8.8m apart — so it must be excluded from the setup's bone-length identity check and compensated in the transplanted action.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/batch_retarget.py#L247-L309",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf95f98ba3239cc7e0f3630f37040a9623914def03680027bd066dfc99e429b3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/README.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:a658b8690db951993eec84b191a0d7c82cc879fb34be7e0a0bb5580f4ea0223e"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_54b1354abdff41f29baae2a89de65851",
      "statement": "batch_retarget.py finds a setup's three armatures by role rather than by name — the Rokoko target scene property is the model, the single armature carrying bone constraints is the cleaned skeleton, and whatever those constraints point at is the source — so a new dataset's blend only has to be wired correctly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/batch_retarget.py#L72-L110",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:769e6f7a2eb145e810650af70c2be4716538db4b846e68343f80561af339001a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c0dd7c4ac3924ffd8d25e8a8f1c5eb42",
      "statement": "A retarget setup's pose bones use euler rotations in whatever order the source BVH declares its rotation channels in — ZYX for LAFAN and ZXY for Bandai-Namco — which is why the cleaned skeleton must be made by duplicating the source object, so the per-bone rotation mode travels with it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/batch_retarget.py#L328-L345",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f5aa6e829efa38f7e384535115bbb0f2b4178704fe914008c2a4ff531759378e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/README.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:a658b8690db951993eec84b191a0d7c82cc879fb34be7e0a0bb5580f4ea0223e"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ae62541fa04a477094d196f4929a85fd",
      "statement": "batch_retarget.py holds every retargeted clip's action on an NLA strip until a single export at the end of the run and accumulates Rokoko rest-pose drift on the model rig, so memory and drift both grow with clip count and reset only when the Blender process exits.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/batch_retarget.py#L364-L392",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6a0dd976ca57dd5a282ecb75dfa26e49bc73dda9e3908a086da0e71c7d0ca368:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/batch_retarget.py#L581-L651",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6a7f4d7b2b8f52e4f94839522d20d89825c9818b2e16d3d0fda94134fc88df00:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8eceb328bf83443ca83116ae23cc97e4",
      "statement": "run_batch_all.py retargets a whole dataset by splitting it into shards along the dataset's own motion labels and running one Blender process per shard, which bounds peak memory, resets rest-pose drift per shard, makes an interrupted run resumable by skipping shards whose FBX exists, and allows shards to run in parallel.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/run_batch_all.py#L116-L146",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:15a29e5f921f6ab477af947b34b79d61569f075ec3eb280514c850638a842126:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/run_batch_all.py#L201-L276",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d6ab09318b0a3ec82675a926400f0f2d308a1f2816ff05ae5d96b909b57ead5e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9050b32bfc4b4c8d96af6ceb016d3f10",
      "statement": "batch_retarget.py compares bone lengths only over the bones named in the Rokoko bone list, because a BVH root's length is the offset down to the first real joint and records capture placement rather than the actor's proportions; measuring it rejected 2,058 of Bandai-Namco dataset-2's own 2,902 clips as belonging to another subject.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/batch_retarget.py#L279-L309",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:800ed1716a5a3b1e63ed85f0cf3d1dbcd11e22cc7aed936ada80ae4d2a7392d9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6033b230ccc6461d89628da34d17d17d",
      "statement": "Because the batch transplants only a BVH's action onto the setup's source skeleton, a clip whose rest offset differs from the setup's is re-framed by exactly that difference; --keep-capture-position compensates the location curves and is off by default so LAFAN's intended normalisation is unchanged.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/batch_retarget.py#L192-L227",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:74e6c8a8c2b1fe38024cf2443a9a3d43b5aacbfd89142e380b7bcbc74db6bde1:"
        },
        {
