    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d3fb96dcc9f34f0fa1f2df5bd42437b0",
      "statement": "How a clip file name maps to a shard label is a named scheme chosen with --shard-by rather than inferred, because Bandai-Namco's dataset_motion_style_index and LAFAN's action_subject conventions both separate fields with underscores and cannot be told apart from a name alone; the action scheme strips the trailing take number so walk1 through walk4 share one shard, and ignores the performer because every LAFAN subject was retargeted onto one skeleton before release.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/run_batch_all.py#L41-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d6a12ea27fa199d5682d73fc40955678e67e540b27aa74a0d33750b3ff45d640:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/run_batch_all.py#L78-L98",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:de89a93c77d1d0b711237cbf831d0935325481df7014523cd7c6fa6aa664a520:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d6a889a23ca140d6b5ae292c2a445b65",
      "statement": "A LAFAN shard's peak memory is governed by frames rather than clip count, because its clips average 6,450 frames against Bandai-Namco's ~133, so the per-shard clip cap has to be set roughly twenty times lower to keep a shard's working set comparable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Tools/Retargeting/run_batch_all.py#L100-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a5f380c8c4a887cc90b14c29bcf744414ac3878b8058df382f112eb4a3ea5b9:"
        },
        {
